# GitHub issue #14

**Repository:** alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus
**URL:** https://github.com/alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus/issues/14
**State:** OPEN
**Labels:** ready-for-agent
**Title:** Room phase model (prefactor)

## Body
## What to build

Prefactor for single-use rooms. The room's lifecycle becomes a single synced `phase` field — `lobby | countdown | playing | ended` — replacing the `hasGameStarted` boolean. Every transition goes through one method on the room, and a `reusable` room option decides what `ended` leads to.

In this ticket `reusable` preserves today's behaviour (`ended` → `lobby`, so "Play Again" in the same room still works) and `countdown` is declared but unused. No player-visible change.

`reusable` is the hook for future private friend rooms (`ended` → `lobby`, `setPrivate()` + join by code); do not build private rooms here.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `phase` is synced in the room state; `hasGameStarted` is removed
- [ ] All phase changes go through one transition method; invalid transitions are ignored
- [ ] `reusable` room option exists and drives what `ended` leads to
- [ ] Existing tests migrated from `hasGameStarted` to `phase` and green
- [ ] Gameplay behaviour unchanged

## Blocked by

None (can start immediately). Client counterpart alexisNorthcoders/snake-phaser#91 must follow before the two are deployed together.
